- **r1** — SSH (tcp/22) drop only; nothing about internet forwarding

The ISP-side RFC1918 filter on `ispa`/`ispb` is suspicious — if r1 is not NAT-ing, private source addresses from PC1 would be dropped there. But the 0-packet counters suggest either NAT is working or traffic never reaches the ISPs at all.

→ **Phase B: routing/control-plane check.** I need to understand how r1 is forwarding and whether NAT is present.
